# On the Run-Time Optimization of the Boolean Logic of a Program.

**Authors:** Cadolino, C., Guazzo, M.

## Abstract
Considers problem of optimal scheduling of Boolean expression (each Boolean variable represents binary outcome of program module) on single-processor system. Optimization discussed consists of finding operand arrangement that minimizes average execution costs representing consumption of resources (elapsed time, main memory, number of input-outputs). Sixteen references and program examples are appended. (EJS)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ286913

